# Source: https://github.com/hoffmangroup/segway/issues/22
#   https://genome.ucsc.edu/goldenPath/help/bigBed.html
# Symptom: first blockSize in the blockSizes list is 0; bedToBigBed rejects
#   with "BED blockSizes must be greater than 0, blockSize[0] = 0".
#   This is distinct from bad/block_size_zero.bed which has a zero-size block
#   somewhere in the middle; here the pathology is specifically that the FIRST
#   block is zero, arising from Segway/segmentation tools that emit 0-origin
#   block offsets instead of sizes.
chr1	0	8000	seg001	1000	.	0	8000	217,95,2	3	0,2000,2000	0,4000,7999
